From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:24:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 35/99] v8: e2k: join instructions into shared wide commands

An instruction no longer owns a 32-byte slot. The layer keeps the last
wide command of the code and puts the operations of the next instruction
into it when that keeps the meaning: they must not read a register or a
predicate the command writes, must not write one it writes, must not
touch memory after its store, and nothing joins a command that loads
(measured slower). Otherwise the command goes right after the last one.
The end of the code is rewritten in place, so it always ends on a slot
boundary and every position anyone can know is still a slot boundary.

Joining stops when the position has been asked for (pc_offset() marks
the slot closed: labels, return addresses, relocations), inside
BlockTrampolinePool scopes, where instructions are counted, and around
instructions that use their own address or are patched: branches,
pcaddi, li64, nop.

Memory accesses of one command go in channel order: a load placed above
a store sees the new value, so joined loads are kept below the store.

Assembler::li is a constant that is not patchable and can join.

E2K_NO_FUSE=1 gives a slot per instruction as before, E2K_FUSE_STATS=1
prints the totals at exit, =2 also who emitted instructions that found
the slot closed. The embedded blob shrinks from 18.4 to 12.4 MB.
